WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.546
This is a recorded native Hermes run with fictional customers.

00:00:04.566 --> 00:00:06.551
It uses public hooks.

00:00:06.571 --> 00:00:10.368
Model tool calls and forced boundary checks are shown separately.

00:00:12.368 --> 00:00:16.281
First, the unbound Northwind job updates Contoso.

00:00:16.301 --> 00:00:21.800
That customer ID is valid, so the tool returns success while the business target is wrong.

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:26.298
Bind the job to its current JSON.

00:00:26.318 --> 00:00:29.130
A forced wrong-customer call is blocked.

00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:33.376
The native model reads SourceBind’s current record and updates Northwind.

00:00:35.376 --> 00:00:40.547
Now Northwind’s source changes from N W forty-one to N W forty-two.

00:00:40.567 --> 00:00:44.904
The old ID is blocked; reading the current source supplies the new one.

00:00:46.904 --> 00:00:49.797
A broken source blocks the protected update.

00:00:49.817 --> 00:00:54.632
Repairing the JSON restores a ready current read while preserving the existing binding.

00:00:56.632 --> 00:01:00.078
Install SourceBind through Hermes’s plugin command.

00:01:00.098 --> 00:01:06.374
The public repository includes the MIT source, the native demo, and the recorded results.

00:01:06.394 --> 00:01:08.848
Read the installation disclosures there.
